\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 G. Leidinger, \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Meisterwerke der Buchmalerei. M\u252 \'fcnchen 1920, S. 16, 29 u. Taf. 28. \endash  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 P. D\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 \rquote \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Ancona, \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  La miniature italienne du Xe au XVIe si\u232 \'e8cle. Paris / Br\u252 \'fcssel 1925, S. 31, Anm. 3. \endash  Biblioteca Universitaria Bologna. Mostra di manoscritti e incunabuli del Decretum Gratiani (Ausst. Kat.). Bologna 1952, Kat. 6. \endash \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24  Sydow\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , S. 227f. \endash \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24  H\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 \u246 \'f6\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 rmann, \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Kat. 62. \endash  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 M. Rotili, \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  La miniatura gotica in Italia, Bd. 1. Neapel\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24  1968, S. 71. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 \endash \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24  Melnikas\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Bd. 1 (Abb. S. 134, 164, 191, 213, 239, 271, 303, 322), Bd. 2 (Abb. S. 349, 380, 457, 653, 774), Bd. 3 (Abb. S. 937, 1083) und passim. \endash  F. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 D\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 \rquote \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Arcais, L' \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 \u8222 \'84\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Illustratore\rdblquote  tra Bologna e Padova. In: Arte Veneta 31, 1977, S. 27-41 (bes. Abb. 12 u. Anm. 5). \endash  F. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 D\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 \rquote \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Arcais, \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Le miniature del Riccardiano 1005 e del Braidense AG.XII.2. Due attribuzioni e alcuni problemi. In: Storia dell\rquote arte 33, 1978, S. 112-114, Abb. 8, 32.\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 \endash \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24  E. Cassee, \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  The missal of Cardinal Bertrand de Deux. A study in 14\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 th\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  -century Bolognese miniature painting. Florenz 1980, S. 115f., Abb. 114-117. \endash  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Conti 1981\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , S. 91. \endash  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 E. Remak-Honnef, \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  in: Thesaurus librorum (Ausst. M\u252 \'fcnchen). M\u252 \'fcnchen 1983, Kat. 48. \endash  M. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Medica, \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 \u8222 \'84\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Miniatori-pittori\ldblquote : il Maestro del Gherarduccio, Lando di Antonio, il Maestro del 1328 ed altri. Alcune considerazioni sulla produzione miniatoria bolognese del 1320-30. In: Francesco da Rimini e gli esordi del gotico bolognese [Ausst. Kat. Bologna], hrsg. von \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 R. D\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 \rquote \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Amico, R. Grandi \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  und \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 M. Medica\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . Bologna 1990, S. 102-105, 123. \endash  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 J. de Veer-Langezaal, \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  A cutting illuminated by the Illustratore (Ms. 13) and bolognese miniature painting of the middle of the fourteenth century. In: The J. Paul Getty Museum Journal 20, 1992, S. 129 u. Abb. 10. \endash  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 R. Suckale, \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Die Hofkunst Kaiser Ludwigs des Bayern. M\u252 \'fcnchen 1993, S. 187, Anm. 62. \endash  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 F. Soetermeer, \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Utrumque ius in peciis: aspetti della produzione libraria a Bologna fra due e trecento. Mailand 1997, S. 270, Anm. 22. \endash \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24  S. Battistini\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , in: DBMI, S. 529f. \endash  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Murano\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , S. 344, 351f. \endash  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 M. Bollati, \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  in: Giotto e le arti a Bologna, Kat. 37. \endash  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 S. L\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 \rquote \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Engle, \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Master of B 18, the Roermond Volumen Parvum, and early fourteenth-century illumination in Bologna. In: Codices manuscripti 52/53, 2005, S. 87f., 93f. }

